          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "# This program displays information about a specific city.\n# It uses variables to store data and the print() function to show it.\n\n# --- Current City Information ---\ncity = \"Tokyo\"\ntemperature = 25\n\nprint(\"Welcome to:\", city)\nprint(\"The current temperature is:\", temperature, \"degrees Celsius.\")\n\n# -----------------------------------\n# Your turn! Make changes below this line.\n\n# TODO 1: Change the 'city' variable to your favorite city.\n# For example: city = \"London\"\n\n\n# TODO 2: Change the 'temperature' variable to a new number.\n# For example: temperature = 15\n\n\n# TODO 3: Modify the print() statements above or add a new one below\n#         to display additional information about your chosen city.\n#         For example: print(\"Population:\", \"9 million\")\n\n\n# TODO 4: Add comments (lines that start with a #) explaining what changes you made.\n# Example: # I changed the city to my hometown.\n",
